            <description><![CDATA[<h2>ChainLink 0.3.687</h2>
<p class="sub">A more reliable update system — plus everything from 0.3.684.</p>

<h3>Updates you can trust</h3>
<p>ChainLink's built-in updater has been rebuilt to need <strong>no credentials at
all</strong> — the update feed and the downloads are now plain public files. If a
download ever fails, you'll see a clear error instead of silence, and nothing
that expires can ever switch your updates off again.</p>

<p><strong>If your copy stopped offering updates recently:</strong> that was a
one-time fault on our side (an expired access key in older builds). Re-download
ChainLink once from your original invite link, drag it to Applications, and
you're permanently back on automatic updates — your data is untouched.</p>

<h3>Recently added (0.3.684)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Modules</strong> — Settings → Modules lets you switch off the parts of
  ChainLink you don't use, per device. Data stays safe and synced.</li>
  <li><strong>Share bike builds</strong> — export a build as a file for a friend;
  import theirs from the Bikes page.</li>
  <li><strong>Smarter plans</strong> — public holidays respected automatically,
  self-scheduling ramp/CP tests, honest session completion, no phantom workouts.</li>
  <li><strong>Pull to refresh</strong> with a stretching dotted indicator, and a
  faster app throughout (shared power curve, lighter Rides page).</li>
</ul>

<h3>A note about Strava</h3>
<p>As of 30 June 2026, Strava requires an <strong>active Strava subscription</strong>
for the API access ChainLink's Strava connection uses. Syncing through
<strong>Garmin Connect</strong> is unaffected and remains recommended.</p>
]]></description>
